assistant_message.content:
First, determine the mowing speed in each mode.

\[
\text{Turtle mode speed}= \frac{\text{area}}{\text{time}}=\frac{600\ \text{m}^2}{55\ \text{min}}
      =\frac{600}{55}\ \text{m}^2/\text{min}
      \approx 10.909\ \text{m}^2/\text{min}.
\]

\[
\text{Rabbit mode speed}= \frac{600\ \text{m}^2}{45\ \text{min}}
      =\frac{600}{45}\ \text{m}^2/\text{min}
      =13.\overline{3}\ \text{m}^2/\text{min}.
\]

A “standard” speed for the mower is usually taken as the average of the two operating speeds:

\[
\text{Standard speed}= \frac{10.909\ \text{m}^2/\text{min}+13.\overline{3}\ \text{m}^2/\text{min}}{2}
   =\frac{(600/55)+(600/45)}{2}
   =\frac{600}{2}\!\left(\frac{1}{55}+\frac{1}{45}\right)
   =300\!\left(\frac{45+55}{55\cdot45}\right)
   =300\!\left(\frac{100}{2475}\right)
   =\frac{30000}{2475}\ \text{m}^2/\text{min}
   \approx 12.121\ \text{m}^2/\text{min}.
\]

If we express this in more conventional units (square meters per hour):

\[
12.121\ \text{m}^2/\text{min}\times 60\ \frac{\text{min}}{\text{h}}
   \approx 727.3\ \text{m}^2/\text{h}.
\]

\[
\boxed{ \text{Standard mowing speed} \approx 12.12\ \text{m}^2/\text{min}\;(\text{or }727\ \text{m}^2/\text{h}) }
\]
